Z||000012||mrfiero||07-22-2001||03:03 AM||||I'm not getting one either and I'm glad I'm not.  Most people don't realize this, but any money you get now from this "rebate" will be taken off of any tax refund you might get next April.<P>If you get $600 now and your tax refund next year is $600 you'll get back $0.  If your refund is $500 then you'll owe $100, etc., etc.<P>It really isn't a rebate so much as it's an advance on your 2001 refund.<P>Happy spending!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula88||07-23-2001||11:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>I'm not getting one either and I'm glad I'm not.  Most people don't realize this, but any money you get now from this "rebate" will be taken off of any tax refund you might get next April.<P>If you get $600 now and your tax refund next year is $600 you'll get back $0.  If your refund is $500 then you'll owe $100, etc., etc.<P>It really isn't a rebate so much as it's an advance on your 2001 refund.<P>Happy spending!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How do you figure this?  As I understand it, it's a refund on my 2000 taxes.  So even if I receive it in 2001, it shouldn't have any effect on my 2001 taxes.  Please correct me if I'm wrong.  I'd like to know where you got your info.  That's the first I've heard of it being an advance.<P>||||reg||5
